module paed-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The Eastern District of Pennsylvania's own civil periods, computed under
// FRCP 6(a), which governs a period stated in a local rule. Rules that
// state no period, or one this layer cannot count, stay out: the notice
// before unsealing (LR 5.1.5), the change-of-address notice (LR 5.1), the
// habeas and section 2255 periods (LR 9.3 to 9.5), the exemption of a case
// with no defense appearance within 120 days from a scheduling order (LR
// 16.2), which sets no filing period, the custody of exhibits and video
// recordings (LR 39.3, 39.3.1), the arbitration scheduling notices and
// pre-hearing exchanges (LR 53.2), which run from notices the clerk sends,
// the payment of costs (LR 54.1(b)), the age of a warrant of attorney (LR
// 56.1) and attorney admission and discipline (LR 83.5, 83.6). The page
// limit on a section 2255 memorandum (LR 9.4) belongs to a habeas package,
// not this civil layer. The Oct. 8, 2024 order amending LR 40.1 adds a
// case-assignment category and states no period. The earlier E.D. Pa.
// outline's FRCP flow belongs to lit/frcp and lit/frap; its decisions
// (Twombly, Iqbal, Foman v. Davis, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Frow
// v. De La Vega, Catlin, Bowles v. Russell, and in the Third and Fourth
// Circuits Phillips v. County of Allegheny, Fowler v. UPMC Shadyside,
// Poulis v. State Farm, Goines and Anderson v. Foundation for Advancement)
// are FRCP authority, and no reporter text is vendored, so they are removed
// here.
/// The summonses in a Social Security review issue by CM/ECF; the later of
/// the complaint's filing and the summonses' issuance is the Date of
/// Service (LR 4.1.3(a)(1)).
event SocialSecurityDateOfService()
/// A motion not certified as uncontested is served with its supporting
/// brief (LR 7.1(c)).
event ContestedMotionServed()
/// A post-trial motion is filed (LR 7.1(e)).
event PostTrialMotionFiled()
/// An order is entered (LR 7.1(g)).
event OrderEntered()
/// The moving party's answer is served (LR 14.1(a)).
event MovantAnswerServed()
/// The deputy clerk sends notice that an action with no proceeding
/// docketed for more than one year will be dismissed (LR 41.1(a)).
event InactivityNoticeSent()
/// An order dismissing a settled action is entered (LR 41.1(b)).
event SettlementDismissalEntered()
/// An arbitration award is entered on the docket (LR 53.2(7)(A)).
event ArbitrationAwardEntered()
/// Final judgment is entered (LR 54.1(a)(1)).
event FinalJudgmentEntered()
/// A notice of taxation of costs (form AO133) is served (LR 54.1(a)(4)).
event CostsNoticeServed()
/// The Clerk taxes costs (LR 54.1(a)(7)).
event CostsTaxed()
/// A magistrate judge's order on a 28 U.S.C. § 636(b)(1)(A) matter issues
/// (LR 72.1(IV)(a)).
event MagistrateOrderIssued()
/// A magistrate judge's 28 U.S.C. § 636(b)(1)(B) proposed findings,
/// recommendations or report is served (LR 72.1(IV)(b)).
event MagistrateReportServed()
/// Objections to a magistrate judge's report are served (LR 72.1(IV)(b)).
event MagistrateObjectionsServed()

/// LR 4.1.3(c): the Commissioner, within sixty days of the Date of
/// Service, files and serves a dispositive motion or the Certified
/// Administrative Record, which is deemed an answer.
deadline social-security-response-period: 60.days after SocialSecurityDateOfService() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 4.1.3(c)"

/// LR 7.1(c): unless the court directs otherwise, a party opposing a
/// motion serves a brief in opposition within fourteen days after service
/// of the motion and supporting brief; a party intending to amend under
/// FRCP 15 files a notice of intent within the same fourteen days.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after ContestedMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 7.1(c)"

/// LR 7.1(e): within fourteen days after filing a post-trial motion, the
/// movant orders the trial transcript or files a verified motion to be
/// excused; otherwise the motion may be dismissed for lack of prosecution.
deadline post-trial-transcript-period: 14.days after PostTrialMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 7.1(e)"

/// LR 7.1(g): a motion for reconsideration or reargument, other than one
/// governed by FRCP 59(e), is served and filed within fourteen days after
/// entry of the order concerned.
deadline reconsideration-period: 14.days after OrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 7.1(g)"

/// LR 14.1(a): leave to join a third party after the FRCP 14 period is
/// ordinarily denied as untimely unless sought within ninety days after
/// service of the moving party's answer.
deadline third-party-joinder-period: 90.days after MovantAnswerServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 14.1(a)"

/// LR 41.1(a): an action noticed for dismissal after more than a year with
/// no proceeding docketed is dismissed with prejudice unless a written
/// application showing good cause is filed within thirty days from the
/// date of the notice.
deadline inactivity-application-period: 30.days after InactivityNoticeSent() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 41.1(a)"

/// LR 41.1(b): an order dismissing a settled action may be vacated,
/// modified or stricken for good cause on an application served within
/// ninety days of its entry, so far as consistent with FRCP 60(c).
deadline settlement-dismissal-vacatur-period: 90.days after SettlementDismissalEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 41.1(b)"

/// LR 53.2(7)(A): within thirty days after the arbitration award is
/// entered on the docket, any party may demand a trial de novo.
deadline trial-de-novo-demand-period: 30.days after ArbitrationAwardEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 53.2"

/// LR 54.1(a)(1), (3): a party requesting taxation of costs files its
/// notice (form AO133) within seventy-five days of the entry of final
/// judgment, unless the court orders otherwise; failure waives costs. The
/// period after an appeal or post-judgment motion (LR 54.1(a)(1), (2))
/// runs from a determination this layer does not model.
deadline costs-notice-period: 75.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 54.1(a)"

/// LR 54.1(a)(4): objections to the bill of costs are filed with the Clerk
/// within fourteen days of service of the notice of taxation of costs.
deadline costs-objection-period: 14.days after CostsNoticeServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 54.1(a)"

/// LR 54.1(a)(7): a party appeals the Clerk's taxation of costs by motion
/// to the court within seven days of the taxation, under FRCP 54(d)(1).
deadline costs-review-period: 7.days after CostsTaxed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 54.1(a)"

/// LR 72.1(IV)(a): a party may object to a magistrate judge's order on a
/// non-dispositive matter within fourteen days after its issuance, unless
/// the magistrate judge or a judge prescribes a different time.
deadline magistrate-order-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateOrderIssued() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 72.1"

/// LR 72.1(IV)(b): a party may object to a magistrate judge's proposed
/// findings, recommendations or report within fourteen days after being
/// served with it.
deadline magistrate-report-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateReportServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 72.1"

/// LR 72.1(IV)(b): any party may respond to another party's objections
/// within fourteen days after being served with them.
deadline magistrate-objection-response-period: 14.days after MagistrateObjectionsServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Pa. L. Civ. R. 72.1"
